{
  "$comment": "THE ask dock x4 (web packages/ui ask-dock.tsx, desktop crates/ui ask_dock.rs, iOS ExpUI AskDock.swift, Android ui/session/AskDock.kt): the question/plan cards WAITING on the viewer leave the transcript and take the COMPOSER's slot, in the session view AND the thread alike (a thread with one pending card looks exactly like a session). `none` = nothing waits, the composer shows. `single` = THE big card (AskCard + AskPrompt: label, the full body inside the dock, the options, the inline field), composer hidden. `stack` (2+) = compact AskCards (icon + label + the one-line `title`, truncating, + the `caption` session name, + the `open` chevron) stacked `stackGap` apart, oldest first; a tap FOCUSES one: it grows in place into the big card (the dock's height animates over motion `resize` with the standard easing, the new content fades in with the motion-enter recipe at `enter`, decelerate; reduce motion = no height animation, opacity only), only that card answers, and a `back` arrow (ghost icon-xs button, LEADING the card's header row, before the kind icon) returns to the stack; answering returns to the stack (or the last card's `single`). The big card's BODY never exceeds `bodyMaxHeightFraction` of the viewport height: it scrolls inside, the options stay below it. Answered cards stay in the transcript CLOSED. The plan card's options are ONE list x4 (`planOptions`, the claude adapter's ExitPlanMode menu): Yes (primary) / Yes, and start with a fresh context / No, keep planning (opens the feedback field); `sessions.answer` carries `decision` + `fresh`; a decided card names `planDecisionLabel`. A thread feeds the dock `threadPendingAsks` (its plan rows with no decision + unanswered question rows of ANY session in the tree, Conversation order, the asking session's TAB name as caption, nested tabs included, the root = null: `threadSessionNames`); the session view feeds it its one answerable card (caption null). Model = pure `askDock`, `askDockTitle`, `planDecisionLabel`, `threadPendingAsks` (src/ask-dock.ts); mirrors compare the WHOLE expected object. EXP-1280: the plan/question cards are the RICH cards of plan-card.json (pictures inline, choice questions, an inline surface); the dock's big card shows the whole card, the compact rows stay the first plain line of the text; `planOptions` + `sessions.answer` (now with `answers` + `surfaceData`) are unchanged.",
